   "fen": "r1bqk1nr/ppp2ppp/1b1p4/4P3/2B1P3/2N5/PPP2PPP/R1BQK2R b KQkq - 1 7",
   "line": [
    "Bc4"
   ],
   "spoken": "Now a fancy option that lays a trap — whenever there's a standoff between the queens and the kings are still uncastled, and the opponent's pieces are underdeveloped, look for it. The key is that the enemy queen is guarded only by its king. So develop the bishop to c4, and a capture invites a sacrifice on f7 that distracts the king and wins the queen.",
   "kind": "tactic"
  },
  {
   "ply": 14,
   "t": 196,
   "fen": "r1bqk1nr/ppp2ppp/1b6/4p3/2B1P3/2N5/PPP2PPP/R1BQK2R w KQkq - 0 8",
